WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.259
The rest of the block.

2
00:00:01.539 --> 00:00:16.792
Multi-head attention (01:21:59) runs several smaller heads in parallel, for example 6 heads of size 64 for an embedding of 384, concatenates their outputs, and applies a linear projection.

3
00:00:17.072 --> 00:00:20.165
Each head can attend to a different kind of relationship.

4
00:00:20.445 --> 00:00:28.360
The suggested exercise EX1 asks you to batch the heads as an extra tensor dimension, which is how nanoGPT does it.

5
00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:39.435
The feed-forward layer (01:24:25) is an MLP applied to each position independently, widening to 4 times the embedding size and back.

6
00:00:39.715 --> 00:00:46.733
The lecture’s summary of the block is communication (attention) followed by computation (the MLP), repeated.

7
00:00:47.013 --> 00:00:54.757
Residual connections (01:26:48) write each sub-layer as x plus f(x) instead of f(x).

8
00:00:55.037 --> 00:01:05.917
In the backward pass the identity path carries the gradient straight through, so deep stacks remain trainable; this is the ResNet idea (He and colleagues, 2015).

9
00:01:06.197 --> 00:01:13.685
Early in training, when f contributes little, the network behaves like a shallow one and gradually brings each block into play.

10
00:01:13.965 --> 00:01:25.059
LayerNorm (01:32:51, Ba and colleagues, 2016) standardizes each token’s vector across its features, with learned scale and shift.

11
00:01:25.339 --> 00:01:32.293
It’s BatchNorm transposed: no batch statistics, no train and eval difference, no coupling between examples.

12
00:01:32.573 --> 00:01:40.723
The lecture places it before each sub-layer (“pre-norm”), which is the arrangement the GPT-2 paper describes in its section 2.

13
00:01:41.003 --> 00:01:44.459
3, along with a final LayerNorm after the last block.

14
00:01:44.739 --> 00:01:55.853
Dropout (Srivastava and colleagues, 2014) randomly zeroes activations during training, a regularizer the lecture adds when it scales up (dropout 0.

15
00:01:56.133 --> 00:01:57.541
2 in its gpt.

16
00:01:57.821 --> 00:02:05.053
py, with block_size 256, 384-dimensional embeddings, 6 heads, and 6 layers).
